.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Rabin&#x27;s 1980 randomization of Miller&#x27;s test declares n &quot;probably prime&quot; after k random witnesses; for a composite n each witness is fooled with probability at most 1/4, so the error shrinks like 4^{-k}. This script shows the test exposing a Carmichael number that fools Fermat&#x27;s test, measures the error rate against the number of rounds for two hard composites, and certifies a 39-digit prime far beyond trial division&#x27;s reach.">

